    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello, \r\n\r\nI just started using mini-starter and I like it so far. But I'm getting an error (screenshot attached)\r\n when I use the dashboard config that's in the documentation. Just the first option, 'Browse' is not working. All the other options open Telescope just fine. I'm not sure if there's a dependency I could be missing or if this is a bug. Here's the error when I use the 'Browse' option. I also have the Telescope plugin installed. \r\n\r\nE5108: Error executing lua vim/_editor.lua:0: nvim_exec2(): Vim:[telescope.run_command]: Unknown command\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_exec2'\r\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function 'cmd'\r\n        ...y/.config/nvim/plugged/mini.starter/lua/mini/starter.lua:1482: in function 'eval_fun_or_string'\r\n        ...y/.config/nvim/plugged/mini.starter/lua/mini/starter.lua:874: in function 'eval_current_item'\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n\r\nAny help would greatly appreciated,  Thanks!\r\n\r\n![Screenshot from 2023-12-10 21-09-10](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/1668110/a0b362a6-2a3d-49e5-b05b-8c9b444bf7f8)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I just started using mini-starter and I like it so far. But I'm getting an error (screenshot attached)<br>\nwhen I use the dashboard config that's in the documentation. Just the first option, 'Browse' is not working. All the other options open Telescope just fine. I'm not sure if there's a dependency I could be missing or if this is a bug. Here's the error when I use the 'Browse' option. I also have the Telescope plugin installed.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">E5108: Error executing lua vim/_editor.lua:0: nvim_exec2(): Vim:[telescope.run_command]: Unknown command<br>\nstack traceback:<br>\n[C]: in function 'nvim_exec2'<br>\nvim/_editor.lua: in function 'cmd'<br>\n...y/.config/nvim/plugged/mini.starter/lua/mini/starter.lua:1482: in function 'eval_fun_or_string'<br>\n...y/.config/nvim/plugged/mini.starter/lua/mini/starter.lua:874: in function 'eval_current_item'<br>\n[string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any help would greatly appreciated,  Thanks!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1668110/289408222-a0b362a6-2a3d-49e5-b05b-8c9b444bf7f8.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Eekr7lFA8UA7vve9pSIrMaGI0F0Rjq5_63VuoP7VGoA\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1668110/289408222-a0b362a6-2a3d-49e5-b05b-8c9b444bf7f8.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Eekr7lFA8UA7vve9pSIrMaGI0F0Rjq5_63VuoP7VGoA\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2023-12-10 21-09-10\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello,\nI just started using mini-starter and I like it so far. But I'm getting an error (screenshot attached)\nwhen I use the dashboard config that's in the documentation. Just the first option, 'Browse' is not working. All the other options open Telescope just fine. I'm not sure if there's a dependency I could be missing or if this is a bug. Here's the error when I use the 'Browse' option. I also have the Telescope plugin installed.\nE5108: Error executing lua vim/_editor.lua:0: nvim_exec2(): Vim:[telescope.run_command]: Unknown command\nstack traceback:\n[C]: in function 'nvim_exec2'\nvim/_editor.lua: in function 'cmd'\n...y/.config/nvim/plugged/mini.starter/lua/mini/starter.lua:1482: in function 'eval_fun_or_string'\n...y/.config/nvim/plugged/mini.starter/lua/mini/starter.lua:874: in function 'eval_current_item'\n[string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\nAny help would greatly appreciated,  Thanks!",
