        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Woah, thanks for this! It is indeed a semi-issue in 'mini.starter', as this item uses `:Telescope file_browser` command which is not a built-in [for already about two years now](https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim/pull/1453). It was moved to [nvim-telescope/telescope-file-browser.nvim](https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope-file-browser.nvim) which you'd have to install in order to use it.\r\n\r\nI'll think about the best approach to resolve this in 'mini.starter' and update it (hopefully) soon. Besides, it might really need a similar new `sections.pick` which uses ['mini.pick'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-pick.md).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Woah, thanks for this! It is indeed a semi-issue in 'mini.starter', as this item uses <code class=\"notranslate\">:Telescope file_browser</code> command which is not a built-in <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim/pull/1453\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim/pull/1453/hovercard\">for already about two years now</a>. It was moved to <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope-file-browser.nvim\">nvim-telescope/telescope-file-browser.nvim</a> which you'd have to install in order to use it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'll think about the best approach to resolve this in 'mini.starter' and update it (hopefully) soon. Besides, it might really need a similar new <code class=\"notranslate\">sections.pick</code> which uses <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-pick.md\">'mini.pick'</a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Woah, thanks for this! It is indeed a semi-issue in 'mini.starter', as this item uses :Telescope file_browser command which is not a built-in for already about two years now. It was moved to nvim-telescope/telescope-file-browser.nvim which you'd have to install in order to use it.\nI'll think about the best approach to resolve this in 'mini.starter' and update it (hopefully) soon. Besides, it might really need a similar new sections.pick which uses 'mini.pick'.",
